n-call.\n\n- **Service:** The \"payments\" service name wasn't recognized. The failing services were `payments-api` (v5.1.0, degraded) and `payments-worker` (v3.4.0, unhealthy). Both showed an 18% error rate.\n- **First attempt:** I tried to roll `payments-api` back to v5.0.0, its last healthy production release. A human reviewer denied it and said the problem was in `payments-worker`. I didn't retry.\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` went from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, its last healthy production release. A human approved it. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are on v3.3.0, and the error rate is now 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 against `payments-worker`. The summary notes the denied `payments-api` rollback.\n\n`payments-api` is still on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. Someone should confirm whether it's contributing to the errors. I didn't roll it back because the reviewer rejected that action.", "type": "text"}]}]}